## done
#
# ---- verdicts: winoracle (Windows 11, WARP, FL 11_0) x64; x86 identical ----
# (write-up: .docs/audits/2026-09-28-d3d11-contract-audit/area-05-context-state.md)
# Vitreo after the area-05 fix pass matches every line except the two
# CreateBuffer lines: Windows refuses STREAM_OUTPUT|UNORDERED_ACCESS on a
# buffer (E_INVALIDARG), Vitreo creates it, so Vitreo prints eight extra
# SO-vs-UAV lines that Windows cannot reach. That is CreateBuffer validation
# (area 02), not a binding rule.
# Findings used by the fix:
#   ClearState resets IA strides/offsets only through the highest slot that
#   holds a buffer; an SO target unbinds/refuses the IB like a VB; RTV/DSV
#   validation compares VIEW extent (mip-adjusted), array size and sample
#   count, and dropped calls leave OM UAVs bound; start+num past u7 is NOT
#   dropped (the slots are ignored) -- the a05 "start1+num8" drop was the
#   rtv0/uav0 conflict; RTVs at slots >= UAVStartSlot are discarded only when
#   NumUAVs > 0, before the conflict check; CS UAV calls naming a subresource
#   twice are dropped, and a new CS UAV unbinds another CS slot of the same
#   subresource; *SetConstantBuffers1 validates every entry (NULL buffers
#   too) before touching any slot; CreateInputLayout requires every ISGN/ISG1
#   element except SV_VertexID/InstanceID -- read or not, pixel-shader
#   SV_Position included -- accepts signature-only blobs, checks the DXBC
#   hash and TotalSize, rejects InputSlotClass > 1 and explicit offsets not
#   aligned to min(4, format size).
